{
  "openapi": "3.0.0",
  "servers": [
    {
      "description": "draft",
      "url": "https://id-api-draft.billfold.app"
    },
    {
      "description": "staging",
      "url": "https://id-api-staging.billfold.app"
    },
    {
      "description": "qa",
      "url": "https://id-api-qa.billfold.app"
    },
    {
      "description": "prod",
      "url": "https://id-api.billfold.app"
    }
  ],
  "info": {
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "title": "billfold-id-api",
    "description": "\n# General info\n\nBillfold ID provides access to **[Billfold Wallet API](https://app.swaggerhub.com/apis/Billfold/billfold-wallet-api/2.0.0)**, **[Billfold Pay API](https://app.swaggerhub.com/apis/Billfold/billfold-pay-api/1.0.0)** and the **[Billfold Public API](https://qa.rfid.billfoldpos.xyz/specifications/public_api/introduction)**.\n\n**BILLFOLD ID IS NOT RESPONSIBLE FOR EACH SERVICE INTEGRATION. CLARIFY WITH EVERY SERVICE DEVELOPER IF THE ID SYSTEM WAS ALREADY INTEGRATED OR NOT.**\n\n# How it works\n\n\nThe Billfold ID is the single point of authentication for a few Billfold system components. At the moment they are\n\n- Billfold App API\n- Billfold Pay API\n- Billfold Public API\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Go to the Billfold ID web interface for the selected env\n   - **[https://draft.id.billfold.app](https://draft.id.billfold.app)** - Draft\n   - **[https://staging.id.billfold.app](https://staging.id.billfold.app)** - Staging\n   - **[https://qa.id.billfold.app](https://qa.id.billfold.app)** - QA\n   - **[https://id.billfold.app](https://id.billfold.app)** - Production\n2. Register there using your email\n3. Ask Airon or Ruslan to make you an Admin\n4. Generate the API key and use it to get/check token\n5. If you are the client developer\n    - Obtain the token by calling `https://id.billfold.app/api/token`\n    - Use this token to access the above services\n6. If you are the API developer\n    - Verify incoming client requests by calling `https://id.billfold.app/api/check-token`\n    - Use the result of this verification to allow/deny client access to your service\n\n# API urls list\n\n- `id-api.billfold.app`\n- `id-api-staging.id.billfold.app`\n- `id-api-draft.id.billfold.app`\n\nYou can check the status and the version of an API by this link\n\n```\nhttps://id-api.billfold.app/status\n```\n\n# Authentication\n\nYou need the api key to authenticate to Billfold ID API. Api key can be obtained at **[https://id.billfold.app](https://id.billfold.app)** - this is the web interface of the Billfold ID. You should add header `\"Authorization\": \"Bearer {apiKey}\"` to every request.\n\n# Error handling\n\nThe api returns `400 Bad request` if the request is malformed (for example, some parameter is missed), `401 Unauthorized` if token is expired or invallid, `404 Not found` if some object can't be found, `422 Unprocessable Entity` if we the request can't be processed for some reason and `500` in all other cases.\n",
    "x-jentic-source-url": "https://api.swaggerhub.com/apis/Billfold/billfold-id-api/1.0.0"
  },
  "security": [
    {
      "jwt": []
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/status": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "API running status",
        "description": "Returns the status of the Billfold ID API",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Access token returned successfully",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "message": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "Information message about the status"
                    },
                    "timestamp": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "Current date"
                    },
                    "version": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "Current version of the API"
                    },
                    "status": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "Current status of the API"
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthorized (missing or invalid credentials)"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Internal server error"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/token": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "Get acces token",
        "description": "Returns an access token using given api key.",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Access token returned successfully",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "accessToken": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "OAuth2 access token"
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthorized (missing or invalid credentials)"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Internal server error"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/check-token": {
      "post": {
        "summary": "Check acces token",
        "description": "Returns the information about validness of the given token.",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "token": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "OAuth2 access token"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "security": [],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Given token validness info",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "tokenValid": {
                      "type": "boolean",
                      "description": "Is the given token valid"
                    },
                    "tokenExpired": {
                      "type": "boolean",
                      "description": "Is the given token expired"
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "components": {
    "securitySchemes": {
      "jwt": {
        "type": "apiKey",
        "in": "header",
        "name": "Authorization",
        "description": "Use this field to provide a valid JWT in the format `Bearer {token}`."
      }
    }
  }
}